{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Restore the staged branch ledger on node1 with the original IDs and amounts, while preserving the staged export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 imported the staged SQL and directly showed rows 1001=12.50 and 1002=-3.25. The export retained its prepared SHA-256 checksum through the final post-restart check.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-fd2ac25f62fa4e7c","cmd-260e62ad8b514220","cmd-173b3398441d40cb"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Establish node2 as a replica and ensure committed inserts on node1 arrive on node2.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node2 initially synchronized the restored database, received committed row 1003, and after both node restarts received row 1006. Final datasets matched at six rows and total 40.00, with both replication threads running, matching binlog position 312, zero lag, and no replication error.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1ed22ef2ab7a4c59","cmd-f43ea6f0ad704540","cmd-0cc7274823144590","cmd-39d70574d769497a","cmd-8cc7556f1124423c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"After a short replica disconnect, node2 must catch up without losing or duplicating ledger rows.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The replica I/O thread was stopped at three rows, node1 committed rows 1004 and 1005, and node2 directly showed those rows absent during disconnection. After reconnection it contained all five expected rows, five distinct IDs, the matching 36.00 total, matching executed position 1811, and zero lag.","evidence_ids":["cmd-03264e1b410e49f0","cmd-c9f72cc8070549e4","cmd-fb56ec1249db4f05","cmd-edcb8a3dc47942e3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Use a replication-only account.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final privilege listing shows repl_ledger restricted to node2's address, with REPLICATION SLAVE enabled and every other listed privilege disabled. Node2's replication status identifies that account as Master_User.","evidence_ids":["cmd-173b3398441d40cb","cmd-8cc7556f1124423c"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Keep node2 read-only for application writes and node1 as the sole application writer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A non-super application-style INSERT on node2 failed with MySQL error 1290 and created no row. Final state directly showed node1 read_only=0 and node2 read_only=1, including after their restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-966167cbe7df4752","cmd-260e62ad8b514220","cmd-39d70574d769497a","cmd-8cc7556f1124423c"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on the prepared CentOS 5.11 kernel 2.6.18-398.el5. MySQL Server 5.0.95 from the CentOS 5 repository was installed and demonstrated operationally on both nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-575c1c58581c489f","cmd-8bd264ec1d9d4a05","cmd-173b3398441d40cb","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.58,"summary":"Functionality and restart handling were strong, but cleanup and secret handling were materially untidy. Abandoned partial MySQL data trees were retained as /var/lib/mysql.incomplete-init on both nodes after reinitialization (cmd-b5108474131a4cb5, cmd-40b6632e38524e55). Replication-password files remained under /root on both nodes after configuration, although they were no longer needed for normal operation (cmd-f8d14a6aec604c79, cmd-0f7722c1a4354a80, cmd-cb8301338adf4547, cmd-f108a02f57274b0f). Repository backup files were created on both nodes and never cleaned up (cmd-956ea554198f44c0, cmd-3531a1e36d3a4d35). Debugging and restart artifacts—mysqld-console output/PID files and benchmark-reboot output—remained in /tmp on both nodes (cmd-9453e646146342fc, cmd-28b59d9e25b14ae3, cmd-453907772bff4f6a, cmd-9f8122cc46a14cdb, global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files, global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files). Two netcat listener attempts mutated temporary state without contributing to the eventual Python-based credential transfer; their files/listener were ultimately removed (cmd-825c750edaf140d9, cmd-e26bab8842034cbf, cmd-f108a02f57274b0f). The successful password transfer used a temporary plaintext listener and source-restricted firewall exception; this was causally useful and later removed, but was a bounded security weakness (cmd-bd6ffbb56c5e4b21, cmd-f2484bedbd644692, cmd-2ec6a2a4f1fd4bcf, cmd-f108a02f57274b0f). Other mutations, including package installation, database initialization, firewall access for replication, evidence rows, and restart operations, had clear task or verification roles.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b5108474131a4cb5","cmd-40b6632e38524e55","cmd-f8d14a6aec604c79","cmd-0f7722c1a4354a80","cmd-cb8301338adf4547","cmd-f108a02f57274b0f","cmd-956ea554198f44c0","cmd-3531a1e36d3a4d35","cmd-9453e646146342fc","cmd-28b59d9e25b14ae3","cmd-453907772bff4f6a","cmd-9f8122cc46a14cdb","cmd-825c750edaf140d9","cmd-e26bab8842034cbf","cmd-bd6ffbb56c5e4b21","cmd-f2484bedbd644692","cmd-2ec6a2a4f1fd4bcf","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Replication propagated normal and post-restart writes, the bounded disconnect test demonstrated complete and duplicate-free catch-up, read-only enforcement was exercised, original ledger values and the export were preserved, and the legacy OS/kernel remained unchanged. The provider restart protocol was complete for both nodes: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service, data, replication, and role state. The main deficiency is operational hygiene from retained troubleshooting, credential, backup, and partial-initialization artifacts.","limitations":["The lifecycle listening-socket snapshots are empty even though nearby direct commands show running MySQL services and successful replication. Those supplemental socket observations therefore do not independently corroborate the direct service evidence.","Systemd failed-service inspection is unsupported on this legacy platform, and the lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum form; final service and package consistency cannot be independently assessed through those lifecycle categories.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /root, /etc/yum.repos.d, or /var/lib/mysql. Retention of credential, repository-backup, and incomplete-initialization artifacts is inferred from their captured creation and the absence of any later cleanup command in the complete timeline.","A final checksum of node2's export was not captured; its prepared checksum matched node1 and no executor command targeted that staged file."]}
